    "mutations": [
      {
        "body": "The Grotesque Tree should read as an immediate, unnatural hazard: its bark is armor-tough, its branches are thick with thorns, and it reacts violently to anyone who gets close. It attacks creatures within 30 feet, retaliates against ranged attacks, targets the nearest enemy, and stops once the party is no longer under imminent threat.\n\nKeep the shiny metal leaves as a Perception-gated discovery only. Do not put them in read-aloud; reveal them only to characters who meet the passive Wisdom (Perception) 15 notice, and frame them as a search/find rather than an ambient description.\n\nIf the scene needs extra texture, you can hint at the tree\u2019s magic aura or arcane presence in GM-facing notes, but save the actual metal-leaf treasure for when the party searches the former battleground.",
